        <!-- ========== complication slots ==========
             Four slots, well under the format ceiling of eight. Each carries a primaryProvider
             naming its own slot service in the wear module; the component is written from the
             RELEASE application id of the watch app, because the debug build takes a .debug suffix
             and a slot pointing at the debug component would sit empty on a release watch.

             Slots 1-3 fall back to a system provider when their primary is absent; slot 4 falls back
             to EMPTY, as before. The slot services exist only in the noLegal watch build (S3178 store boundary), so the Play
             watch build never offers them, and an EMPTY fallback left a face installed from Play
             with three blank slots for every store user (S3548). Every slot still lists EMPTY,
             which keeps a wearer's own "empty" choice valid.

             Each slot is hidden in ambient. Which of these four the always-on screen should keep is
             still open for the owner to decide (strategic spec 6.7); starting from none makes the
             remaining pixel budget measurable instead of guessed at. -->

        <!-- S3558: every slot's default provider is its own WearFaceSlotN service, which serves the
             option the wearer picked for that position in the phone companion - a watch section, a
             watch program, app data or a system shortcut. One service per slot because a request does
             not say which slot asks. The slots stay customizable, so the system editor can still put
             steps or heart rate there. The answer is always SHORT_TEXT with an icon: a shortcut sends
             an empty text and shows the icon alone, a value shows both. -->

